tags: free-below-load, free_while_scarcity_below

A promise of the node: while the load of each resource is below a threshold, the node
charges nothing for the time of an instance.

The value is the threshold in millionths, from 1 to 1000000, in base 10. Example:
200000. When one resource is at the threshold or above, the node charges its normal
price.

With no promise, the caller assumes that the node always charges. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=promise
load=for each resource in resources: the part of the capacity of the node that is in use, in millionths, as the node measures it
